<!-- WHAT TO BRING -->
<section class="bring">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="bring-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="bring-script">If you decide to admit</span>
        <h2>What to bring (and what to leave at home).</h2>
        <p>Once admissions is approved, we'll walk you through everything in detail. Here's a quick overview to help you plan ahead and reduce the stress of arrival day.</p>
        <p style="font-size:13.5px;color:var(--soft);font-style:italic;">Don't worry about getting this perfect. We have toiletries, clothing, and most essentials on hand if you arrive without something. The goal is to get you here safely — we'll handle the rest.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bring-cols">
        <div class="bring-col">
          <h4>✓ Bring</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Photo ID (driver's license, state ID, passport)</li>
            <li>Insurance card (if applicable)</li>
            <li>List of current medications</li>
            <li>Comfortable clothing for 7–10 days</li>
            <li>Sneakers and comfortable shoes</li>
            <li>Personal hygiene items</li>
            <li>Glasses or contacts if needed</li>
            <li>Small amount of cash for incidentals</li>
            <li>Phone numbers of family/support</li>
            <li>Journal or notebook (optional)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bring-col no">
          <h4>✗ Leave at Home</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Alcohol or any non-prescribed substances</li>
            <li>Weapons of any kind</li>
            <li>Aerosol products</li>
            <li>Mouthwash containing alcohol</li>
            <li>Revealing or offensive clothing</li>
            <li>Large amounts of cash or valuables</li>
            <li>Electronics with internet access (limited use)</li>
            <li>Outside food or drinks</li>
            <li>Items with sentimental value (in case of loss)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- CONTACT FORM -->
