<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="faq-sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="sec-script">Common questions</span>
      <h2 class="sec-h2">About admissions &amp; payment</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item open">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="this.closest('.faq-item').classList.toggle('open')">
          What does "private pay" actually mean for me?
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">Private pay means the cost of treatment is paid directly (by you, your family, or a combination) instead of through insurance. We work hard to make this accessible — with transparent pricing, payment plan options, and honest conversations about what's realistic for your situation. Call us and we'll walk through it together.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="this.closest('.faq-item').classList.toggle('open')">
          How much does treatment cost?
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">Cost depends on the length of stay (30, 60, or 90 days) and the level of care recommended after assessment. Rather than list a number here that may not reflect your actual situation, we prefer to give you accurate pricing when you call — along with payment plan options that can make care affordable.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="this.closest('.faq-item').classList.toggle('open')">
          When will you be in-network with my insurance?
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">Credentialing timelines vary by insurer. Some providers take 60–90 days, others take longer. Call us with your specific insurance and we'll let you know exactly where we are in the process — and whether out-of-network options or future enrollment could work for you.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="this.closest('.faq-item').classList.toggle('open')">
          How quickly can I be admitted?
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">Most clients are admitted within 3–5 days of their first call. In urgent situations we move faster when we can. We don't believe in long waitlists for people who need help now.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="this.closest('.faq-item').classList.toggle('open')">
          Can my family come to admissions with me?
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">Yes. We welcome family involvement at every step — from the first call through admission, treatment, and aftercare. Family healing is part of personal healing. We'll talk through how that looks for your situation.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="this.closest('.faq-item').classList.toggle('open')">
          What if I'm not sure I'm ready?
          <svg fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a">That's okay. Many people who call aren't ready in that moment — they're just exploring. Calling doesn't commit you to anything. We'd rather help you think through your options today than have you wait alone for a perfect moment that may never come.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


